WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.472
The evaluation spans two scales.

00:00:03.552 --> 00:00:07.024
First,

00:00:07.104 --> 00:00:10.575
two synthetic MNIST variants isolate the
phenomenon: a long-tailed ColorMNIST with strong class imbalance,

00:00:10.655 --> 00:00:14.127
and a biased ColorMNIST where each class has a
characteristic hue with tunable spread.

00:00:14.207 --> 00:00:17.679
Then, eight standard image classification benchmarks,

00:00:17.759 --> 00:00:21.231
from CIFAR and STL-10 to Flowers-102, Stanford
Cars, and ImageNet,

00:00:21.311 --> 00:00:24.783
test the method in realistic settings.

00:00:24.863 --> 00:00:28.335
To probe robustness,

00:00:28.415 --> 00:00:31.886
every test image is re-rendered under a gradual hue
shift from minus one-hundred-eighty

00:00:31.966 --> 00:00:35.438
to plus one-hundred-eighty degrees,

00:00:35.518 --> 00:00:38.990
and accuracy is averaged across the full sweep.
